<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <DUT Name="ST_GeneralStatus" Id="{9c22d4f5-1bbc-427a-b513-f8bf1db18bd2}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
ST_GeneralStatus - VAT590 EtherCAT "General Status" readback word.

Purpose:
    Input word carrying the 16 general status bits of the VAT590 needle valve.
    It is read by FB_VCN_VAT590 through i_stGenStatus (AT %I*) and decoded into
    ST_VAT590_STATUS (stValveStatus).

Usage:
    Bit n of this structure is bit n of the valve's General Status process data.
    Map it 1:1 onto the EtherCAT input image and never write to it. The two
    access mode bits are combined into E_VAT590_AccessMode; all Reserved bits are
    unused by this application and shall be ignored by integrators (they are
    documented below so that no bit position is left ambiguous).

Objectives:
    Keep the encoded status and access-mode semantics unambiguous, so the valve
    state cannot be misinterpreted by integrators or from EPICS.

History:
    Janez Govednik      2022-03-17  Created VAT590 EtherCAT interface
    plc-scirix audit    2026-11-28  Added header and per-member bit documentation
*)
TYPE ST_GeneralStatus :
STRUCT
    Bit0FieldBusDatavalid : BIT;  // Fieldbus data valid: TRUE = valve process data (status/warnings) is valid
    Bit1ZeroExecuted : BIT;       // Zero procedure executed: TRUE = zero (close/calibrate) command completed by valve
    Bit2PingPongRxBit : BIT;      // Ping-pong receive bit: echoes Bit2PingPongTxBit of ST_GeneralControlSP (command cycle check)
    Bit3PressureSimulation : BIT; // Pressure simulation active: TRUE = valve simulates the pressure input, real sensor ignored
    Bit4PressureSPReached : BIT;  // Pressure setpoint reached: TRUE = measured pressure is within tolerance of the setpoint
    Bit5Reserved : BIT;           // Reserved (no function): unused VAT bit, always ignore
    Bit6Reserved : BIT;           // Reserved (no function): unused VAT bit, always ignore
    Bit7AccessModeBit0 : BIT;     // Access mode readback bit 0 (LSB) - see Bit8AccessModeBit1
    Bit8AccessModeBit1 : BIT;     // Access mode readback bit 1 (MSB): 00=LOCAL, 01=REMOTE, 10=LOCKED (11 not valid)
    Bit9WarningsActive : BIT;     // Warnings active: TRUE = at least one bit set in ST_GeneralWarnings/ST_ExtendedWarnings
    Bit10Reserved : BIT;          // Reserved (no function): unused VAT bit, always ignore
    Bit11Reserved : BIT;          // Reserved (no function): unused VAT bit, always ignore
    Bit12Reserved : BIT;          // Reserved (no function): unused VAT bit, always ignore
    Bit13Reserved : BIT;          // Reserved (no function): unused VAT bit, always ignore
    Bit14Reserved : BIT;          // Reserved (no function): unused VAT bit, always ignore
    Bit15Reserved : BIT;          // Reserved (no function): unused VAT bit, always ignore
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>